# this is a comment
print("hi")

// Checks whether duso accepts '#' as a comment marker. It does not -- duso
// comments are '//' -- so line 1 fails to lex and this script does not run.
// Kept as a record of that: if '#' comments are ever added, this starts passing.
//
// Named .duso, not .du, on purpose. The tooling only treats .du as source, so
// the pre-commit hook lints every .du file and refuses to commit one that fails.
// This file is supposed to fail, so it gets an extension the linter ignores.
